 "definition": "Summary of the committed LJ-efficiency scans (lj_eff_{real,geom}_<era>.json): per mode, era, channel and efficiency, the per-point (Run 3 - 2018) differences over the 18 grid points as mean, statistical error of the mean (per-point binomial errors propagated), RMS, [min, max], number negative, and the chi2 of the 18 differences about their mean (17 dof). A chi2 far above 17 means the points do not share a common shift, so the mean +- stat is not the uncertainty of one. Also the in-acceptance fractions. Writes lj_eff_summary<tag>.json (--production v1: no tag, the files of the first production; v2, the default: _v2, from lj_eff_{real,geom}_v2_<era>.json, five eras). No EOS access.",
